From: Rosen Penev <rosenp@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ARM: dts: BCM5301X: EA9200: use network LED trigger for WLAN LED

The "rfkill-none" trigger is only registered when CONFIG_RFKILL_LEDS is
enabled, which OpenWrt disables tree-wide, so the WLAN LED never lights
up. Use the network LED trigger instead.

Signed-off-by: Rosen Penev <rosenp@gmail.com>
---
 arch/arm/boot/dts/broadcom/bcm4709-linksys-ea9200.dts | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/arch/arm/boot/dts/broadcom/bcm4709-linksys-ea9200.dts
+++ b/arch/arm/boot/dts/broadcom/bcm4709-linksys-ea9200.dts
@@ -62,7 +62,8 @@
 			color = <LED_COLOR_ID_AMBER>;
 			function = LED_FUNCTION_WLAN;
 			gpios = <&chipcommon 0 GPIO_ACTIVE_LOW>;
-			linux,default-trigger = "rfkill-none";
+			linux,default-trigger = "network";
+			family = "wlan";
 		};
 
 		led-1 {
